---
// A line in a participant's voice --- something people in the room have said
// about a real model --- set as a quoted aside above the figure that answers
// it. Use the block form so MDX treats it as flow content and the quote gets
// its own paragraph inside:
//
//   <Voice>
//   "it wrote something genuinely new---how?"
//   </Voice>
//
// A one-line `<p class="voice">…</p>` is inline JSX inside a markdown
// paragraph, which nests a <p> in a <p>; the browser then splits it into an
// empty paragraph either side of the real one.
---

<div class="voice"><slot /></div>
